{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**The brand sponsor bears the economic shortfall; the contractual investment adviser remains responsible to the fund.**\n\n- **Economic burden:** Under the sponsor’s expense-assumption agreement, the sponsor funds the gap when the revenue allocated to it is insufficient to cover its assumed expenses.\n- **Fund-facing obligation:** The adviser named in the unitary-fee advisory agreement remains obligated to cover the promised fund expenses—even if the sponsor fails to pay. The adviser must perform, then seek reimbursement or other contractual remedies against the sponsor.\n\nExpenses expressly excluded from the unitary-fee arrangement remain payable by the fund.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Delegating payment to a sponsor does not, by itself, release the adviser from its obligation to the fund; the actual contracts control."}}
